Is the CPU used by your application or by another process ? Is it
essentially user or system time ?

If all the CPU is used by by your application process, here is what I
suggest.

Build your app in debug mode (-g). When the problem occurs, attach a
debugger (for instance, ladebug yourapp -pid <pid>).
Then, interrupt the program with Ctrl-C, look at the call stack (bt), then
continue execution (c). Do this several times (Ctrl-C, bt, c). If there is a
loop in your process, you will likely pinpoint the call sequence.
If necessary, step more finely in the code (n).

Hope this helps,

--
Jerome





