Daniel wrote:
> has anyone ever heard or seen a recommended reboot time for tru64
> machines?  just curious.. i know Winders products need at least
> monthly reboots, just did not know if tru64 had a recommended one.

We reboot as needed ie when something catastrophic happens like a key 
piece of software mysteriously locks up etc.  Sometimes restarting a 
piece of software doesn't cut it.

How often you might need to reboot any server (Unix or otherwise) will 
always depend on the bugs present in the O/S or application software. 
So it pretty much comes down to how well was the software written that 
you are using.  Usually it is the applications in our case that cause 
problems.

Why should a reboot fix an application problem on Unix?  Well, honestly, 
it probably isn't required but I've never had the luxury of time to 
trouble-shoot an app to the nth degree when staff are clamoring for the 
thing to start working again.  If restarting the app doesn't work and 
unless it's immediately obvious, I reboot the server and hope that does 
it.  Sometimes it doesn't and then I learn something new about the 
situation and file it for next time.

To give you some idea of Tru64 stability though - I have had servers 
running nearly a year without stopping.  When I first started working 
where I am now, we had a server down for some reason and I realised I 
had never seen it's console boot screen before and I had been there for 
7 months as the Sys Admin.



