The cluster should operate fine if the shared mounts are on a private bus.
Of course if the node that can see the storage goes down you're done...
And performance...

As for the add member problem, I would say yes you can do what I think
you're asking.

Install node A as a single node cluster with an extra disk (node B's boot
disk).   Next run the add member command.  Finally remove the extra disk
from node A and attach it to a bus node B can see.  Then boot node B
from that disk.

Although I have never tried this, I cannot think of any reason why it
shouldn't
work.

