> parent ino:  1198
> inode id:    1224          inode dev:   (2659,253641) [regular file]
> object mode: 0555
> result:      3 (0x3)
> cpu, seq#:   0x0, 34774
> ip address:  175.175.16.152 (lebrun)
> timestamp:   Fri Apr 11 14:00:05.71 2003 CEST
> "
> 
> I there a way that I can know on what TTY this command has been
> launched?
> This way I can use the 'w' cmd with 'ps' to get person that logged on
> 'root' and typed that command.
> (what's does the cttydev field mean?)

The AuditID is an ID assigned to every individual login of a user. If you have 
two separate users logged in as "root" (UID: 0), they will still be assigned 
DIFFERENT AUIDs. So, use that AUID (0 in this case) to track down the login 
event, which will give you the IP address of the client.

Nix.



